  "findings": {
    "observedSequence": "Each first menu frame returns after a long callback; its frame-owned native fence then reports CONDITION_SATISFIED and the menu reveals. The old scheduler starts another automatic complete frame 73.4\u201391.0 ms later. That frame returns and its own fence last reports TIMEOUT_EXPIRED. The original normal click begins 935.343\u20131014.522 ms after reveal and fails its original 15-second stability deadline.",
    "eventLoopBoundary": "Every failed click has 30 streamed timer callbacks with activeCallback 0, fixed native heartbeat count/timestamp and zero screencast frames. Timer intervals remain approximately 496\u2013507 ms. Thus an uninterrupted 15-second application RAF callback is not what this evidence shows; browser RAF delivery is absent while timer tasks continue.",
    "fenceBoundary": "The second fence was genuinely pending at its last native query, shortly before the click. No native queries are observed during the RAF silence; its actual completion time and the specific driver/compositor cause are unknown. No GL finish, extra wait or readback was inserted by this analysis.",
    "stableCheckConnection": "The installed Playwright injected _checkElementIsStable implementation schedules bounding-rectangle comparisons with native requestAnimationFrame. Its dependency on delivered animation callbacks matches the observed original action log stopping at visible/enabled/stable; this does not require inferring moving CSS geometry.",
    "candidateAssessment": "The frozen policy directly targets the observed premature automatic redraw: it retains the admission timestamp across the long draw, reserves recovery proportional to the occupied eligible callback interval after genuine completion, and preserves the original base/following-callback handoff. It changes scheduling rather than per-frame quality or input deadlines. This is a mechanism match, not proof of a successful original browser journey.",
    "candidateScope": "Root confirms no cold precompilation is included in the current frozen candidate. Original menu/settings and MotoGP browser acceptance is still pending; explicit preview transactions and later transitions are not validated by these initial failed clicks.",
    "retentionBoundary": "The 89/101/146 browser-side drops occur in the early preparation burst around page +2.6\u20133.0 seconds, before the first menu frames. No later drop-counter changes, Node ring drops or packet sequence gaps are recorded. Clock anchors are corroborated by matching console packets. Last retained activity is never treated as proof of continued execution beyond capture."
  },
